    "created_at": "2026-02-09T14:29:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-02-09T14:29:45Z",
    "body": "I am worried about implementing `controls` as a singular opt in to \"some user agent controls\". (Perhaps what you could call) consensus among web developers is that `controls` is very coarse grained and it's either \"you get a bunch of buttons at the discretion of the UA\" or \"you reimplement all of those controls in JS\". A happy medium (like that expressed in https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/2293) would be nicer.\n\n\nI'm definitely curious about https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/2293#issuecomment-283698523. @annevk I'd like to dig more into the particulars here - _if_ WebKit are opposed to implementing something like the shape of `controlslist`, what feedback do you have for that proposal, that it might help shape this one? If we could focus on that during the next WHATNOT to move both of these issues forward, I think that could be a productive next step!",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
