    "created_at": "2026-03-03T20:53:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-03T20:53:26Z",
    "body": "No objections from Chromium. I'd characterize our support as neutral since it's unclear what will happen in terms of user and developer expectations when `controls` are not supported. There are no mechanisms for JS based animated image control, so it's hard to make a comparison against `<video>`. Maybe that's an argument for `play()`, `pause()` on `<img>`?",
