    "created_at": "2026-03-16T21:39:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-16T21:39:24Z",
    "body": "I spoke to @dalecurtis about this again, and we'd like to stick to our \"neutral\" position on the API. We're definitely not blocking or vetoing the PR, but the open questions above mean it's unclear we'd want to implement the behavior in isolation, without a more complete developer picture. E.g. this comment\n\n> I think if you want to be in full control of the UI you'll have to do something imperative. \n\nisn't possible to do today for `<img>`, and wouldn't be with the current proposal, would it? Perhaps if [CSS image animation](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-image-animation-1/#w3c-partial) gets shipped, that may be an answer.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
