    "created_at": "2026-03-26T09:33:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-26T09:33:56Z",
    "body": "It seems it's an open question how controlling animated images is expected to work. Having the controls set UA style rules like `image-animation: paused` works, but lets the developer override with their own style rules, which seems easier to do accidentally compared to media elements. If we set `!important` then developer-provided controls instead wouldn't work. Changing CSS rules doesn't seem like ideal DX. If we add methods like `play()` and `pause()`, it needs to be defined how they interact with the CSS property, and how animation grouping works.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/4133066703/reactions",
